E
poor harvest tool~
A length of fraying twine binds together a chipped hand pick, a dull
skinning knife, a nicked hatchet head on a split wooden haft and a patched
gathering sack. Everything here has seen hard use, but it will serve for
mining, forestry, hunting and gathering alike.

Carried or held, this tool guarantees at least poor quality on successful
wilderness harvests. Poor is already the lowest result, so this bundle is
mostly a starting point on the way to better tools. Only your best harvest
tool applies, tools inside containers do not count, and the tool is never
consumed.
~
